00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,360
Whoa, whoa, take it easy.

262
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:39,980
Relax.

263
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,420
Jeez, you're sweating like a pig.

264
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,640
What's going on?

265
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,100
I can't go through with this.

266
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,160
I just can't.

267
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,460
I'm not ready for marriage.

268
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:48,780
What was I thinking?

269
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:50,740
I'm only 35 years old.

270
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,900
I've got my entire life ahead of me.

271
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:53,920
Adventure's waiting.

272
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,220
I can't settle down yet.

273
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:56,940
What are you talking about?

274
00:10:57,340 --> 00:11:05,000
It wasn't more than a month ago that you were rambling on about how you are tired of living the life of a bachelor and how you envy your friends that have a family.

275
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:05,660
I know.

276
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,000
Let's think this through.

277
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,560
First of all, you cannot leave Amy at the altar.

278
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:17,820
Not only will she be humiliated and kill you, but she's the woman that you love and the woman of your dreams.

279
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:20,400
Why would you want to end that or jeopardize it like this?

280
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,060
Second of all, you were just getting cold feet.

281
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:26,140
You know deep down inside that you'd want to marry her.

282
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:27,620
So cut the crap and do it.

283
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:28,480
You're right.

284
00:11:28,950 --> 00:11:29,670
I'm being crazy.

285
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:31,250
Okay, I'm ready.

286
00:11:31,850 --> 00:11:32,290
Let's do this.

287
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:33,110
Great.

288
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:34,880
Phew.

289
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:35,880
That was a close one.

290
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:36,950
You had me going there for a minute.

291
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:39,470
I thought I was going to have to slap some sense into you.

292
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,560
Alright, so this is a popular scenario, right?

293
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:54,160
Everybody on their wedding day, they get cold feet and they back out.

294
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,620
TV, movies, books, everyone loves this situation.

295
00:11:57,240 --> 00:12:06,070
Have you ever actually heard of or experienced or maybe known of somebody who actually left the bride at the altar or the groom at the altar?

296
00:12:06,290 --> 00:12:07,470
I don't know anyone who did that.

297
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,720
Luckily, I think it's really sad.

298
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,720
Yeah, me neither.

299
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,710
I don't think it's really that common.

300
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:13,830
No, but there was a movie just about this.

301
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:24,680
So there's a woman, Julia Roberts, who tries and tries and tries to get married but never can so it's called Runaway Bride because every time she goes to the altar, she gets nervous.

302
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:26,620
She gets cold feet and she runs away.

303
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,600
They call her the Runaway Bride.

304
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,680
I can't imagine this actually happening to someone.

305
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:33,060
I mean, you have all your family there, your friends.

306
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,080
I know.

307
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:34,660
It'd be so embarrassing.

308
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:35,400
It's amazing.

309
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:36,480
And expensive.

310
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,100
Exactly, because you've already paid for everything.

311
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,080
So do you get to eat the cake if you're the one who's left behind?

312
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,180
I think so.

313
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,340
Everything's paid for, right?

314
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:44,740
Exactly.

315
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,600
And drink all the liquor.

316
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,660
Alright, so that's all the time we have for today.

317
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:53,920
If you have any questions, any comments, you can come to our website at EnglishPod.com and we'll see you guys there.

318
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:54,560
Bye everyone.

319
00:12:54,920 --> 00:13:03,151
Bye.
